    "title": "Private symbols in `__all__` break the Python convention that underscore-prefixed names are internal. `_cap_body` and `_format_findings_section` were not in `__",
    "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> Private symbols in `__all__` break the Python convention that underscore-prefixed names are internal. `_cap_body` and `_format_findings_section` were not in `__all__` before this split, and tests can import them directly without them appearing here. Including them makes `from lintro.ai.review.github import *` expose two implementation-detail helpers as if they were public API.\n\n```suggestion\n__all__ = [\n    \"STATE_MARKER_PREFIX\",\n    \"STICKY_MARKER\",\n    \"MAX_COMMENT_CHARS\",\n    \"build_sticky_comment\",\n```\n\nNote: If this suggestion doesn't match your team's coding style, reply to this and let me know. I'll remember it for next time!\n\n<a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/ide/cursor?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20lintro%2Fai%2Freview%2Fgithub.py%0ALine%3A%2047-53%0A%0AComment%3A%0APrivate%20symbols%20in%20%60__all__%60%20break%20the%20Python%20convention%20that%20underscore-prefixed%20names%20are%20internal.%20%60_cap_body%60%20and%20%60_format_findings_section%60%20were%20not%20in%20%60__all__%60%20before%20this%20split%2C%20and%20tests%20can%20import%20them%20directly%20without%20them%20appearing%20here.%20Including%20them%20makes%20%60from%20lintro.ai.review.github%20import%20*%60%20expose%20two%20implementation-detail%20helpers%20as%20if%20they%20were%20public%20API.%0A%0A%60%60%60suggestion%0A__all__%20%3D%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%22STATE_MARKER_PREFIX%22%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%22STICKY_MARKER%22%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%22MAX_COMMENT_CHARS%22%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%22build_sticky_comment%22%2C%0A%60%60%60%0A%0AHow%20can%20I%20resolve%20this%3F%20If%20you%20propose%20a%20fix%2C%20please%20make%20it%20concise.&pr=1481&platform=github\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCursorDark.svg?v=6\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCursor.svg?v=6\"><img alt=\"Fix in Cursor\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCursor.svg?v=6\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20lintro%2Fai%2Freview%2Fgithub.py%0ALine%3A%2047-53%0A%0AComment%3A%0APrivate%20symbols%20in%20%60__all__%60%20break%20the%20Python%20convention%20that%20underscore-prefixed%20names%20are%20internal.%20%60_cap_body%60%20and%20%60_format_findings_section%60%20were%20not%20in%20%60__all__%60%20before%20this%20split%2C%20and%20tests%20can%20import%20them%20directly%20without%20them%20appearing%20here.%20Including%20them%20makes%20%60from%20lintro.ai.review.github%20import%20*%60%20expose%20two%20implementation-detail%20helpers%20as%20if%20they%20were%20public%20API.%0A%0A%60%60%60suggestion%0A__all__%20%3D%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%22STATE_MARKER_PREFIX%22%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%22STICKY_MARKER%22%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%22MAX_COMMENT_CHARS%22%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%22build_sticky_comment%22%2C%0A%60%60%60%0A%0AHow%20can%20I%20resolve%20this%3F%20If%20you%20propose%20a%20fix%2C%20please%20make%20it%20concise.&repo=lgtm-hq%2Fpy-lintro&pr=1481&platform=github\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaudeDark.svg?v=6\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\"><img alt=\"Fix in Claude Code\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/ide/codex?prompt=IMPORTANT%3A%20Work%20in%20the%20repository%20%22lgtm-hq%2Fpy-lintro%22%20on%20the%20existing%20branch%20%22refactor%2F1113-split-oversized-modules%22.%20Checkout%20that%20branch%20%E2%80%94%20do%2