    "title": "The `plugin` parameter is accepted but never referenced inside `doc_url` — the function only uses `code`. Every other helper in this module genuinely needs `plu",
    "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> The `plugin` parameter is accepted but never referenced inside `doc_url` — the function only uses `code`. Every other helper in this module genuinely needs `plugin` to access class state, so the extra parameter here is misleading and makes the function harder to call or test in isolation.\n\n```suggestion\ndef doc_url(code: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Return TypeScript error documentation URL.\n\n    Uses typescript.tv, a third-party error reference, since the\n    official TypeScript handbook does not provide per-error pages.\n\n    Args:\n        code: TypeScript error code (e.g., \"TS2307\" or \"2307\").\n\n    Returns:\n        URL to the TypeScript error documentation, or None if invalid.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not code:\n        return None\n    # Strip \"TS\"/\"ts\" prefix if present to get the numeric portion\n    upper = code.upper()\n    num = code[2:] if upper.startswith(\"TS\") else code\n    if num.isdigit():\n        return DocUrlTemplate.TSC.format(code=num)\n    return None\n```\n\nNote: If this suggestion doesn't match your team's coding style, reply to this and let me know. I'll remember it for next time!\n\n<a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/ide/cursor?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20lintro%2Ftools%2Fdefinitions%2F_ts_checker_command.py%0ALine%3A%20176-196%0A%0AComment%3A%0AThe%20%60plugin%60%20parameter%20is%20accepted%20but%20never%20referenced%20inside%20%60doc_url%60%20%E2%80%94%20the%20function%20only%20uses%20%60code%60.%20Every%20other%20helper%20in%20this%20module%20genuinely%20needs%20%60plugin%60%20to%20access%20class%20state%2C%20so%20the%20extra%20parameter%20here%20is%20misleading%20and%20makes%20the%20function%20harder%20to%20call%20or%20test%20in%20isolation.%0A%0A%60%60%60suggestion%0Adef%20doc_url%28code%3A%20str%29%20-%3E%20str%20%7C%20None%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%22%22%22Return%20TypeScript%20error%20documentation%20URL.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20Uses%20typescript.tv%2C%20a%20third-party%20error%20reference%2C%20since%20the%0A%20%20%20%20official%20TypeScript%20handbook%20does%20not%20provide%20per-error%20pages.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20Args%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20code%3A%20TypeScript%20error%20code%20%28e.g.%2C%20%22TS2307%22%20or%20%222307%22%29.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20Returns%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20URL%20to%20the%20TypeScript%20error%20documentation%2C%20or%20None%20if%20invalid.%0A%20%20%20%20%22%22%22%0A%20%20%20%20if%20not%20code%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20return%20None%0A%20%20%20%20%23%20Strip%20%22TS%22%2F%22ts%22%20prefix%20if%20present%20to%20get%20the%20numeric%20portion%0A%20%20%20%20upper%20%3D%20code.upper%28%29%0A%20%20%20%20num%20%3D%20code%5B2%3A%5D%20if%20upper.startswith%28%22TS%22%29%20else%20code%0A%20%20%20%20if%20num.isdigit%28%29%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20return%20DocUrlTemplate.TSC.format%28code%3Dnum%29%0A%20%20%20%20return%20None%0A%60%60%60%0A%0AHow%20can%20I%20resolve%20this%3F%20If%20you%20propose%20a%20fix%2C%20please%20make%20it%20concise.&pr=1481&platform=github\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCursorDark.svg?v=6\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCursor.svg?v=6\"><img alt=\"Fix in Cursor\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCursor.svg?v=6\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20lintro%2Ftools%2Fdefinitions%2F_ts_checker_command.py%0ALine%3A%20176-196%0A%0AComment%3A%0AThe%20%60plugin%60%20parameter%20is%20accepted%20but%20never%20referenced%20inside%20%60doc_url%60%20%E2%80%94%20the%20function%20only%20uses%20%60code%60.%20Every%20other%20helper%20in%20this%20module%20genuinely%20needs%20%60plugin%60%20to%20access%20class%20state%2C%20so%20the%20extra%20parameter%20here%20is%20misleading%20and%20makes%20the%20function%20harder%20to%20call%20or%20test%20in%20isolation.%0A%0A%60%60%60suggestion%0Adef%20doc_url%28code%3A%20str%29%20-%3E%20str%20%7C%20None%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%22%22%22Return%20TypeScript%20error%20documentation%20URL.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20Uses%20typescript.tv%2C%20a%20third-party%20error%20reference%2C%20since%20the%0A%20%20%20%20official%20TypeScript%20handbook%20does%20not%20provide%20per-error%20pages.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20Args%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20code%3A%20TypeScript%20error%20code%20%28e.g.%2C%20%22TS2307%22%20or%20%222307%22%29.%0A%0A%20%20%20%20Returns%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20URL%20to%20the%20TypeScript%20error%20documentation%2C%20or%20None%20if%20invalid.%0A%20%20%20%20%22%22%22%0A%20%20%20%20if%20not%20code%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20return%20None%0A%20%20%20%20%23%20Strip%20%22TS%22%2F%22ts%22%20prefix%20if%20present%20to%20get%20the%20numeric%20portion%0A%20%20%20%20upper%20%3D%20code.upper%28%29%0A%20%20%20%20num%20%3D%20code%5B2%3A%5D%20if%20upper.startswith%28%22TS%22%29%20else%20code%0A%20%20%20%20if%20num.isdigit%28%29%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20return%20DocUrlTemplate.TSC.format%28code%3Dnum%29%0A%20%20%20%20return%20None%0A%60%60%60%0A%0AHow%20can%20I%20resolve%20this%3F%20If%20you%20propose%20a%20fix%2C%20please%20make%20it%20concise.&repo=lgtm-hq%2Fpy-lintro&pr=1481&platform=github\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaudeDark.svg?v=6\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\"><img alt=\"Fix in Claude Code\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/ide/codex?prompt=IMPORTANT%3A%20Work%20in%20the%20repository%20%22lg